WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.940
At a branch, the question
is where traffic leaves

2
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:05.975
the building and what
enforces policy when it does.

3
00:00:05.975 --> 00:00:07.400
There are four patterns.

4
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.575
The hairpin is assessed but slow.

5
00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:12.225
Bare breakout is fast, and a regression.

6
00:00:12.225 --> 00:00:14.769
Governed breakout, with
an edge device and a

7
00:00:14.769 --> 00:00:17.738
nearby security service,
is the reference pattern.

8
00:00:17.738 --> 00:00:21.081
And agent-based SASE suits
small or roaming sites,

9
00:00:21.081 --> 00:00:24.663
as long as the nearest point
of presence really is near.

10
00:00:24.663 --> 00:00:29.011
The guidance is to choose per site
from measured latency and device mix,

11
00:00:29.011 --> 00:00:31.075
and never to choose bare breakout.

12
00:00:31.075 --> 00:00:33.500
Five decisions carry most of the risk.
